{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"communication and operator surface clarity","packet_sha256":"daa8d78a88ab7201a9a29877c96d58f4c1815f8b9c6f56cd303981efa217e7a5","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"7f0311e26d5963157a9bc6ad5f0f3ecdf4c5c686849ce610b33c34380f04a82f","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"CLARITY-001","severity":"blocker","summary":"The documented freeze flow requires reading the intended provider parent, but the freeze CLI never performs or accepts that readback; it constructs parent identity solely from --parent-repo and --parent-number.","evidence":["skills/public/achieve/SKILL.md: approval and identity says to read the intended parent before freezing.","skills/public/achieve/scripts/goal_binding_freeze.py: parent_identity() constructs the URL and identity directly from CLI arguments; run_freeze() passes that synthetic value as expected_parent.","No provider adapter, parent read command, or parent-readback input is present in the reviewed CLI surface."],"action":"Either make freeze explicitly a post-readback command by requiring and validating a provider-read parent identity, or revise the documentation and operator messaging to state that provider parent verification is an external prerequisite and expose the verification artifact clearly."},{"id":"CLARITY-002","severity":"blocker","summary":"The --binding-path option is presented as an override, but any non-deterministic path is rejected during validation and the success output always reports the deterministic sibling.","evidence":["goal_binding_freeze.py help text says '--binding-path Binding path (default: the draft's deterministic .binding.json sibling)', implying custom paths are supported.","goal_binding.py _validate_payload() rejects any binding whose path is not binding_path_for_draft(draft_path).","goal_binding_freeze.py run_freeze() passes the custom target to write_immutable_binding(), so a custom path predictably refuses as path-invalid."],"action":"Remove --binding-path or make it genuinely supported; align help, implementation, error behavior, and emitted binding_path before release."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The freeze command has typed YAML success/refusal output and tests cover help, successful creation, malformed manifests, missing drafts, and immutable attempt reuse.","bin":"real-but-nonblocking","disposition":"These improve operator diagnostics but do not resolve the misleading parent-authority and binding-path contract."},{"concern":"The documentation is detailed and names the bootstrap, attempt-id, cursor, and observation concepts.","bin":"real-but-nonblocking","disposition":"The breadth of documentation does not compensate for the two contradictory operator contracts identified above."}],"next_move":"Repair the freeze CLI contract and its documentation together, then add focused tests for parent-readback provenance and custom binding-path behavior before re-review.","non_claims":["No live provider execution or host-rendered reviewer receipt was available in the packet.","This review does not assess implementation behavior outside the supplied semantic payload.","The verdict is based on operator-facing contract contradictions, not on inferred current-workspace state."]}
